\section{Method}
\subsection{Task Definition}
Based on the above studies, this paper focuses on the task of multimodal sarcasm detection and proposes a novel multimodal sarcasm recognition framework. 
This task aims to determine whether multimodal content composed of both text and image expresses sarcastic semantics.

Formally, let $T = \{t_1, t_2, \ldots, t_n\}$ denote the input text sequence, and let $V$ denote the corresponding image. 
The objective of this task is to learn a mapping function:

\begin{equation}
f(T, V) \rightarrow y
\end{equation}


where $y \in \{0, 1\}$ represents the sarcasm label, with $y = 1$ indicating sarcastic content and $y = 0$ indicating non-sarcastic content.




